{"claim": "The recall result shape is the orient contract: {claim, detail, tags, confidence, home, time, age_days, stale, stale_checked, promoted, score}. Callers (the executive first) depend only on this shape; recall internals are free to change behind it. No CONTEXT_CTL seam exists - seams are reserved for fillers that cross ownership or delivery lines (owner call 2026-08-15).", "tags": "phase1", "confidence": "high", "time": 1786810992022},
{"claim": "adjudicate is the only sanctioned write path for extracted claims: remember stays the raw append (validation, audience guard, dedupe), adjudicate wraps it with belief dynamics - use remember for deliberate session deposits, adjudicate for anything machine-extracted. The result shape {status, action: settled|corroborated|contradicted|superseded|inserted, target, before, after, reasoning} is contract like recall's.", "tags": "phase3", "confidence": "high", "time": 1786815210574},
{"claim": "The audience guard was removed 2026-08-15 (owner's reversal): remember refuses nothing based on tags or readers lists. Local instances are sovereign - curation happens at the credentialed exits (repo push rights, crates.io tokens, branch-diff review of promote/seed/package changes), never by policing local writes. Earlier manual claims describing the guard are historical.", "tags": "correction", "confidence": "high", "time": 1786821663861},
{"claim": "H5 landed: the drive's act repertoire - reverify (the curator: confirm re-stamps the source hash so stale CLEARS, amend = decay + remember with fresh stamp, retire = decay; the one act that fixes staleness rather than just acknowledging it), connect (notions into kb.notions, never self-promoted), wonder (open questions into the runtime wonderings record, capped 20), all rotating 2/1/1/1(+distill) on the idle tick after consolidate_room's free try, with epistemic_work+decay as the no-frontier floor. Every deposit rides adjudicate/remember so curation traces feed the curriculum automatically - rumination trains the model", "detail": "Live battery on the CLAUDECODE arm: reverify confirmed both genuinely-stale claims (kb.frontend shadow-root, agent.llm providers) with referent-grounded reasoning - stale 2 -> 0, hash re-stamped, traces journaled with author reverify. connect produced a real insight (the salience curriculum's selection bias toward previously-unparseable cases - checkable, stated nowhere). wonder surfaced two owner-grade questions incl. the code-why 1026-vs-4 distillation gap. Corroboration in adjudicate does NOT refresh source hashes - that is reverify's write, deliberately.", "tags": "harvest,h5,rumination", "confidence": "high", "time": 1787146055993},
{"claim": "Shipped memory facets clash with git in two distinct ways (owner-raised 2026-08-21, unresolved): curation machinery (adjudicate confidence steps, reverify re-stamps, decay, trace appends) mutates TRACKED canon bytes as a side effect of merely operating, and a facet being one canonically-serialized JSON array in one file makes concurrent memory changes on two branches a guaranteed textual conflict even when the semantic merge (union by exact-claim dedupe) is trivial.", "detail": "The intended design already routes learnings through the instance-local brain with promote as the only door to shipped manuals - the defect is that curation does not obey it: adjudicate/reverify/decay rewrite shipped facets in place and traces land on the target control, dirtying canon (observed live: the archivist writing manuals onto dev library records; the new git sensor now correctly announces this dirt every ~30s - the sensor is right, the write path is wrong). Brainstormed but NOT decided: promote-only enforcement, an instance-owned memory.local overlay facet with copy-on-write confidence deltas, entry-per-file content-addressed layout (union-merges free), or JSONL append-log with merge=union where confidence changes are superseding lines. Same disease class as the removed cmd/ tracking.", "tags": "agent.archivist,kb,memory-facets,git,canon-hygiene,merge,unreviewed", "confidence": "high", "time": 1787317812100},
{"claim": "epistemic_work's unpromoted branch never consults the promoted stamp, so every claim promote has ever stamped generates promotion pressure forever.", "detail": "Observed on a fresh brain: epistemic_work reported unpromoted:8 while all 8 subject-bearing claims already carried promoted timestamps (agent, agent.executive, agent.archivist, agent.sensor, dev.code...). Reading the source, the last branch tests only e.has(\"subject\"). Running agent-archivist-promote cannot clear it - exact-claim dedupe makes it a no-op and the count is unchanged - so the queue can never converge. The fix is one condition: `if !pushed && e.has(\"subject\") && !e.has(\"promoted\")`. Pre-existing, not a bootstrap failure; a fresh brain with a promoted primer just makes it visible.", "tags": "agent.archivist,epistemic_work,promote,bug,work-queue,unreviewed", "confidence": "high", "time": 1787255981879},
{"claim": "Almost no claim in the federation carries a bindable source pointer, so the staleness/decay machinery has nothing to act on.", "detail": "Census of all 206 live claims (2026-08-21): 95 with no source at all, 110 with a {doc: ...} pointer, and exactly ONE with the full {lib,ctl,facet,hash} shape remember stamps and hashes. Only facet-pointer sources can drift, so epistemic_work reports stale: 0 and decay - the executive's single autonomous write - is effectively dead code in practice; sensor-bound claims on a store_change perception likewise read last_bound: 0. The ratio will move, but the structural cause is durable: doc pointers and sourceless claims are unbindable by construction, so binding coverage is the lever, not the decay ladder.", "tags": "agent.archivist,agent.executive,kb,staleness,decay,epistemic_work,binding,unreviewed", "confidence": "medium", "time": 1787308200520},
{"claim": "Brick 3 landed (overlay commit 6c4b288, claude/git-first-class): memory claims can bind git-repo sources - a {repo, path} source stamps the working-tree FNV hash (same algorithm as facet sources, the load-bearing staleness field) plus the HEAD commit as provenance, and a bare {doc} pointer that resolves inside exactly ONE registered repo is auto-upgraded to a checkable repo pointer at remember time.", "detail": "The whole staleness pipeline speaks the shape: recall byte-compares repo sources against the working tree (unregistered repo or vanished file reads stale); epistemic_work and decay's drift test handle both shapes procedurally, so the stale/decay loop works on repo-bound claims with the resident model off; reverify re-reads repo referents (confirm re-stamps hash AND commit, amend keeps the source shape); all five canonical serializers (adjudicate included) carry the repo/path/commit field order so rewrites stay byte-stable. Verified live end-to-end: a wrong-hash claim made epistemic_work report its first-ever real stale item, decay stepped high->medium once and no-oped on repeat. This is the fix for the earlier findings that almost no federation claim carried a bindable source pointer - the {doc} upgrade path targets the ~110 previously-unbindable claims.", "tags": "agent.archivist,dev.git,staleness,source-pointers,epistemic-work,unreviewed", "confidence": "high", "time": 1787315970309},
{"claim": "Shipped memory domains are promote-only (one-memory-cycle A1/A2/B2): remember, adjudicate, decay and reverify route deposits and curation deltas for any library whose data/<lib> is tracked inside a registered git repo to the instance-local overlay at runtime/agent/memory-overlay/<lib>.<ctl>.jsonl, and curation traces go to <lib>.<ctl>.traces.jsonl unconditionally; recall, epistemic_work, the sensors and the model readers read the union (facet in legacy-array or JSONL form, overlay lines superseding by exact claim); agent-archivist-promote is the only writer of shipped facet bytes and rewrites them as a line-oriented JSON array (one canonical object per line, every entry line comma-terminated, closed by a constant {\"end\": true}] terminator) - valid single-document JSON for the store loader, line-mergeable via .gitattributes *.memory merge=union. Normal operation therefore never dirties a tracked repo.", "tags": "memory,overlay,promote,one-memory-cycle", "confidence": "high", "time": 1787319737606},
{"end": true}]
